HOW THE ACCURACY CALCULATOR WORKS
=================================

This describes how the site works out its numbers. The base game rules it starts
from are in the "accuracy formula" file.

Code: src/data/accuracy.js (all the math), src/pages/AccuracyCalculator.jsx (the page),
src/components/AccuracySummary.jsx (the right panel).


WHAT THE PAGE SHOWS
---------------------------------------
Levels bar: the chance the selected gags kill each cog level, with two exceptions:
  Only lure, or only lure and trap: the lure's accuracy, labelled "Lure hit chance"
  Any other single track: that track's accuracy, labelled "Gag Accuracy"
Trap alone has no accuracy of its own, so it stays on "Chance cog dies".

Right panel: each track's chance to hit at 3 cog levels (11, 12, 13 by default), plus
Cog dies. The arrows move the levels 1 at a time, from 1-3 up to 18-20.

Clicking a track's row in the right panel marks it as already hit. See ALREADY HIT below.

Up to 5 gags can be selected, same as the damage calculator.


STEP 1: ONE TRACK'S ACCURACY
---------------------------------------
atkAcc = propAcc + trackExp + tgtDef + bonus, capped at 95%

propAcc: the gag's base accuracy
trackExp: always 60
tgtDef: from the cog's level (level 12 is -55, level 13 is -60, level 14 and up is -65)
bonus: see below

Each track rolls once, so all the gags in a track hit or miss together.

Bonus:
  +25 for each gag that hit in an earlier track (a stun)
  +50 for every track after a lure springs a trap
  +10 to the lure if a trap is placed, +5 for each extra trap
  Trap placements and successful lures give no stun

Tracks always go in this order: trap, lure, sound, throw, squirt, drop.


SPECIAL CASES
---------------------------------------
Trap: never rolls by itself. It only goes off if the lure hits, so it shows the lure's
chance. With no lure it shows "-" and deals no damage. If there are several traps, only
the first one deals damage.

Multiple lures: the highest lure sets the accuracy and each lower or equal lure adds a bonus.
  +10 for $1 bill or small magnet
  +15 for $5 bill or big magnet
  +20 for $10 bill, hypno goggles or presentation
  Bills mixed with magnets, hypnos or presentation give no bonus
  With 3 or more lures, every extra lure adds its bonus

Lured cog: the next track always hits (100%) and knocks the cog out of the lure.
The exception is drop, which can't hit a lured cog (0%) and leaves it lured.
This only happens if the lure hit, so the track's chance mixes both outcomes (see Step 2).

SOS: an SOS always hits, so its whole track shows 100%, even with normal gags in that track.
  The SOS itself gives no stun, but normal gags in its track still do
  An SOS drop hits a lured cog (the damage calculator still says it misses)
  An SOS trap shows 100% but gives no lure stun or +50 bonus, and only deals damage if a lure hits


STEP 2: WALKING EVERY OUTCOME
---------------------------------------
A track's accuracy depends on what hit before it, so one fixed number per track isn't
enough. Instead the calculator goes through every combination of hits and misses, which
is at most 32 per level (5 tracks, 2 outcomes each). It's exact, not an estimate.

For each combination:
  1. Chance of it happening: multiply each track's hit or miss chance together
  2. Damage dealt: add up only the tracks that hit

Then:
  Track accuracy = the chances of every combination where that track hit, added up
  Cog dies = the chances of every combination where damage reaches the cog's health, added up

Results are rounded to the nearest whole percent. Above 99% they keep 1 decimal
(e.g. 99.8%), and 100% only shows when it's certain.


DAMAGE RULES (same as the damage calculator)
---------------------------------------
Track damage: all the gags in the track added up
Combo: +20% of that if the track has more than 1 gag (rounded up)
Knockback: +50% of it for the throw or squirt track that hits a lured cog (rounded up)
Trap: the trap's damage when the lure hits. No knockback when a trap is used

The accuracy page has no modifiers, so Damage Up, Overpaid and the rest aren't included.


EXAMPLE 1: LURE THEN THROW (LEVEL 12)
---------------------------------------
$1 bill + birthday cake

Lure: 60 + 60 - 55 = 65%
Throw on its own: 75 + 60 - 55 = 80%

Throw always hits if the lure hit, and rolls its 80% if the lure missed:
  Throw = (0.65 x 1) + (0.35 x 0.80) = 0.93 = 93%

Cog dies: the cake deals 150 with knockback, which is short of level 12's 196 HP, so it's 0%.


EXAMPLE 2: COG DIES (LEVEL 14, 254 HP)
---------------------------------------
2 birthday cakes + fire hose + grand piano

Damage:
  Cakes: 100 + 100 + 20% combo = 240
  Hose: 30
  Piano: 170

Accuracy:
  Cakes: 75 + 60 - 65 = 70%
  Hose: 95 + 60 - 65 = 90%, or 95% after the cakes hit (+50, capped)
  Piano: 50 + 60 - 65 = 45%, plus 25 for each gag that already hit:
    Cakes and hose hit: 95% (capped)
    Cakes hit: 95%
    Hose hit: 70%
    Nothing hit: 45%

Cakes  Hose  Piano  Chance                        Damage  Dies?
Hit    Hit   Hit    0.70 x 0.95 x 0.95 = 63.175%  440     Yes
Hit    Hit   Miss   0.70 x 0.95 x 0.05 =  3.325%  270     Yes
Hit    Miss  Hit    0.70 x 0.05 x 0.95 =  3.325%  410     Yes
Hit    Miss  Miss   0.70 x 0.05 x 0.05 =  0.175%  240     No
Miss   Hit   Hit    0.30 x 0.90 x 0.70 = 18.900%  200     No
Miss   Hit   Miss   0.30 x 0.90 x 0.30 =  8.100%   30     No
Miss   Miss  Hit    0.30 x 0.10 x 0.45 =  1.350%  170     No
Miss   Miss  Miss   0.30 x 0.10 x 0.55 =  1.650%    0     No

Cog dies = 63.175 + 3.325 + 3.325 = 69.825%, shown as 70%

The 8 chances always add up to 100%, which is a handy check.

The 2 cakes alone would be 0% here, because 240 is short of 254. The hose and piano are
what make the kill possible.

The same gags at other levels:
  Level 12: 95%
  Level 13: 75%
  Level 14: 70%
  Levels 15-18: 66%
  Level 19: 63%
  Level 20: 0%


EXAMPLE 3: TNT
---------------------------------------
TNT + $1 bill. TNT deals 180, so it kills level 11 (156 HP) but not level 12 (196 HP).

Level 11: lure is 60 + 60 - 50 + 10 (trap) = 80%, so Cog dies = 80%
Level 12: 180 is less than 196, so Cog dies = 0%

TNT with no lure never goes off, so Cog dies is 0% at every level.


ALREADY HIT
---------------------------------------
Clicking a track's row marks it as already hit: the row turns green with a check in its
dot, and its accuracy becomes 100% at every level. Clicking again undoes it.
It counts as a normal hit: it deals its damage and gives later tracks their stun. A lure
marked as hit also lures the cog or springs the trap, and a drop marked as hit lands even
on a lured cog.

Trap rows can't be clicked because trap follows the lure, and SOS rows can't because
they're already 100%. Removing every gag from a track clears its mark.

Example 2 at level 14 with the cakes marked as hit: the bottom 4 rows of the table can no
longer happen, so Cog dies = 0.95 + (0.05 x 0.95) = 99.75%, shown as 99.8%.


LEVELS BAR COLOURS
---------------------------------------
Green at 90% or higher, light green for any lower chance, red at 0%
When the bar is showing accuracy: green at 95% or higher, light green from 80%, red below 80%
Grey when no gags are selected
